--- !u!1001 &471771706
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 1773053956}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 1300172517041989184, guid: cbdd694e559e34a7e923b7e6f8a81336, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Classification: Internal Use Only

        Document ID: H-73/0421-IC

        Originating
        Department / Laboratory: Cognitive Systems Research Unit


        Induction
        of Controlled Cognitive Synchrony in Human Subjects


        This study
        documents the controlled induction of prolonged unconscious states in multiple
        adult participants. Subjects were placed under pharmacologically maintained
        comas and sustained using standard ventilatory support. Neural activity was
        modulated via a centralized device designed to produce uniform cortical oscillations.
        Continuous monitoring was conducted to ensure synchronization across subjects.
        Data recorded includes electroencephalographic patterns, autonomic stability,
        and variance reduction in higher-order brain activity.













        One
        subject exhibited brief arrhythmic fluctuations during initial induction,
        resolved without intervention. Uniformity remained intact thereafter. Long-term
        effects remain undetermined.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1300172517041989184, guid: cbdd694e559e34a7e923b7e6f8a81336, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
